 "translation": "You ask, 'What shall I do for the lord of the great mountain of waterfalls and Kino trees?' My friend with a beautiful forehead! If I do not take your words as a mere joke, what will become of you out of worry for me?",
 "modern": "அருவிகளும் வேங்கை மரங்களும் நிறைந்த பெரிய மலைநாட்டிற்கு உரிய தலைவனுக்காக, \"நான் என்ன செய்வேன்?\" என்று நீ கேட்கிறாய். அழகிய நெற்றியை உடைய தோழியே! உன்னுடைய அந்த வார்த்தையை நான் ஒரு விளையாட்டாக எடுத்துக் கொள்ளவில்லை என்றால், என் நிலைமையைக் கண்டு வருந்தி நீ என்ன பாடுபடுவாய்?",
 "explanation": "In this Kuriñci poem, the heroine addresses her close friend who is deeply anxious about the hero's delay in marrying her. The friend asks in despair, 'What shall I do to help you with the lord of the mountain?' The heroine, touched by this deep empathy, replies that if she were to take this question seriously instead of treating it as a lighthearted joke to ease the tension, the friend would be consumed by unbearable grief. The mountain landscape, with its cascading waterfalls and blooming Kino trees, represents the rich but currently distant world of the hero. Key words like 'nakai' (joke/laughter) and 'naṉṉutal' (beautiful forehead) highlight the tender, protective bond between the two women.",
